course: dictionary
lesson: 9733
title: Sunlight and what it does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sunlight is the light that comes from the Sun. It is a compound word, made from two smaller words, sun and light, so the word itself gives you a clue. «Plants need sunlight to make their food.»
explain: Sunlight can also mean a place or time where this light falls. «She was sitting in the sunlight by the window.» Here the author means where the light is, not the light itself. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Sunlight is uncountable, so we say some sunlight or more sunlight, never two sunlights. To check your meaning, swap in «the light from the Sun» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Sunlight means the light that comes from the Sun.
fact: Sunlight is uncountable, so we say some sunlight, not a sunlight.
fact: Plants need sunlight to make their food, in a process called photosynthesis.
fact: Sunlight takes about eight minutes to reach the Earth, and white sunlight splits into the colours of the rainbow.
fact: Too much sunlight burns skin, so use sun cream, a hat and shade, and never look straight at the Sun.
exercise: «Plants need sunlight to make their food.» What does sunlight mean here? | Water from the rain | Soil and worms | Wind blowing through the leaves | *The light that comes from the Sun
exercise: «She was sitting in the sunlight by the window.» Here, sunlight means | Very hot water | A type of sun cream | A cloudy sky | *A place where the Sun's light falls
exercise: Sunlight is made from two smaller words. Which two? | *sun and light | sunny and right | son and light | sun and lit
test: Too much sunlight burns your skin. What should you use to stay safe? | *Sun cream, a hat and shade | A thick winter coat in summer | Jumping into cold water | Ice cubes on your arms
test: Which sentence uses sunlight correctly? | The sunlights are very tall. | Two sunlights came through the window. | We bought a sunlight from the shop. | *We need some sunlight to help the plants grow.
exam: In the dark deep sea, fish glow with their own light because «sunlight never reaches» that far down. What does this tell us? | Fish dislike sunlight, so they hide in the dark | Sunlight reaches every part of the ocean | Sunlight is brighter at night than in the day | *Sunlight does not reach the deepest parts of the ocean, so fish must make their own light
